1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
"I paid, but nothing arrived." — every online seller gets this message. The agent asks one SQL door (Zetaris) across the PSP ledger, orders, grants, server logs and mail events.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Case 1 — the PSP says PAID, our order row says failed. The chain breaks at "Order confirmed", and the raw rows that prove it are one click away.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Case 2 — paid, but the confirm call never arrived. Same symptom for the customer, different broken link, different evidence.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Case 3 — the customer got the credits twice. Two grant rows, one timeout, one manual retry.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Case 4 — credits granted, mail never sent. The customer has them and does not know. Reply draft, fix (needs approval), dispute evidence bundle.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Case 5 — nothing is broken. You were never charged. The agent can say so, with evidence.
